      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you—when the effort feels like it’s all for nothing, stopping can seem like the only honest choice. But \"less of a fight\" isn't the same as \"better\"—it's just a quieter kind of pain. You don’t have to build a house on sand; you can just sit in the sand and let it be, one breath at a time. The hollow feeling isn't a sign you're wrong—it's a sign you're tired, and that's okay to honor without giving up.",
